.TH ZERODDS-SNITCH 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-snitch \- DDS discovery probe (SPDP / SEDP snapshot)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-snitch
[\fBprobe\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-snitch
joins a DDS domain, listens for SPDP and SEDP traffic for the duration
of
.B \-\-duration
(default 5s), then prints all discovered participants plus
publication / subscription endpoint counts.
.PP
The
.B probe
sub-command is implicit when the first argument is a flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Probe duration: \fI5\fR, \fI30s\fR, \fI2m\fR, \fI1h\fR. Default: 5s.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format:
.I text
(default) or
.I json.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
The base configuration file; its sibling
.IR PATH .d/
holds drop-ins. Default: the system configuration directory
.RI ( /etc/zerodds
on Linux,
.I /usr/local/etc/zerodds
on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-spy (1),
.BR zerodds-monitor (1)
